<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vandal conquest of North Africa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">429–439 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vandal conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> was the seizure of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and Alans between 429 and 439 CE. Crossing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> under King Gaiseric, they captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in 439 and established a kingdom that controlled much of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a> profile places this disruption of Roman North Africa in the context of the Garamantes' decline.</p></div>
